    output
      label = Output
      type = select
      remember = true
      defaultValue = None
      options
        None
        White Background
          value = white background
        Monochrome
          value = monochrome, black and white tones
        Multiviews
          value = presented in multiple views or angles
        Reference Sheet
          value = structured reference sheet with labeled views
        Vintage
          value = retro style with cel shading and old-school coloring
        Pop Art
          value = bright, bold colors and thick outlines inspired by comic books
        Magazine Cover
          value = styled like a high-fashion magazine cover
        Cartoon
          value = simplified, exaggerated cartoon-style illustration
        Sketch
          value = raw pencil or ink sketch style, unpolished
        Painting
          value = textured, brush-stroked painterly finish
        Watercolor
          value = soft watercolor paint effect with flowing tones
        Comic Panel
          value = presented as part of a comic book panel
        VHS Effect
          value = grainy, low-res style with VHS scanlines and noise
        Posterized
          value = minimal color gradients with hard edges, poster-like
        Glitch
          value = visual distortion with digital glitch artifacts
        Pixel Art
          value = low-resolution pixel-based retro graphics
        Line Art
          value = clean black and white outlines with no coloring
        Neon Glow
          value = elements glowing in neon light, cyberpunk vibe
        Blueprint
          value = blueprint-style technical drawing on a grid background

